Thu Nov 12 08:46:19 UTC 2026 - Андрей Алыпов <and.november@opensuse.org>

- Update to version 0.50.0:
- Added
  * Options::max_depth and DEFAULT_MAX_DEPTH to configure the maximum
    nesting depth when parsing.
  * The path attribute on textPath (SVG 2).
- Changed
  * The bounding box methods of Node, Group and Path now return an Option,
    which is None for nodes without a bounding box, such as empty groups.
    resvg_get_node_bbox and resvg_get_node_stroke_bbox of the C API return
    false for such nodes, --query-all skips them, and --query-bbox fails
    for an SVG without content.
  * The underline, overline and line_through fields of layout::Span are now
    boxed.
  * Bounding boxes of paths and groups are now calculated on first access
    instead of while parsing.
  * Fonts are now loaded, resolved and prepared for shaping once per tree
    instead of once per text, and fonts with shared data are no longer
    copied.
  * Lower memory usage of the parsed tree and lower peak memory usage while
    parsing.
  * Faster parsing of documents with many IDs.
  * harfrust updated to 0.15 and skrifa to 0.49.
  * svgtypes is now developed in the resvg repository.
- Fixed
  * flood-color="currentColor" on feFlood and feDropShadow no longer
    resolves to black.
  * color="currentColor" now inherits the parent's color instead of
    resolving to black.
  * Filter primitive subregions with primitiveUnits="objectBoundingBox" are
    now resolved against the element's bounding box, and unspecified values
    default to the filter region.
  * feDisplacementMap no longer applies scale twice, and now reads the
    displacement map with non-premultiplied colors.
  * CSS in a style element is no longer cut off at the first XML comment or
    processing instruction, and a type attribute that is empty or text/css
    in any letter case is now accepted.
  * Recursive references through clip paths, masks, patterns, markers and
    feImage, including indirect ones via nested elements and inherited
    properties, are now detected and rejected.
  * usvg no longer hangs on an xlink:href chain that loops without
    including its first element.
  * Placement of sbix bitmap glyphs.
  * Patterns with fractional tile sizes no longer drift out of position or
    show seams between tiles.
  * An empty group no longer extends the bounding box of its parent group.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Oct 26 12:01:47 UTC 2026 - Андрей Алыпов <and.november@opensuse.org>

- Update to version 0.49.0
- Added
  * --query-bbox CLI option to query the drawing bounding box without
rasterizing it.
  * mix-blend-mode: plus-lighte.
  * feComposite operator="lighter.
  * Prebuilt aarch64 release binaries for Linux and Windows.
- Changed
  * usvg::BlendMode and usvg::filter::CompositeOperator have new
    PlusLighter and Lighter variants.
  * Group::layer_bounding_box of a group without filters is now clipped by
    its clip path, so clipped groups allocate smaller layers. This also
    affects the sizes reported by --query-all and used by --export-id.
- Fixed
  * dominant-baseline is now correctly inherited by nested <tspan>
    elements, so a nested span stays on the same baseline as its siblings.
  * Panics and incorrect clipping when a filter region is smaller than its
    input.
  * Incorrect transform order on the outermost svg element with a viewBox.
  * Relative positioning of right-to-left text with dx and dy, including
    text on a path and text decorations.
  * text-anchor now uses the actual extent of a text chunk, which dx and
    textLength can change.
  * Filters inside rotated or skewed groups are now applied in the user
    space of the group. This fixes the clipping to filter regions and
    subregions, as well as the direction of offsets, blurs, turbulence and
    tiles, and the rendering of feImage.
  * gradientTransform and patternTransform are now inherited via href.
  * The bounding box of an <image> with preserveAspectRatio="… slice" is
    now its viewport, so objectBoundingBox clip paths, masks and filters on
    it are resolved correctly.
  * Markers are now clipped to their viewport instead of their viewBox when
    the aspect ratios differ.
  * Object bounding box gradients inside masks, patterns and feImage
    filters used by more than one element are now resolved correctly,
    instead of being rendered as a flat fill or not at all.
  * feMorphology kernels are now symmetric and fractional radii are rounded
    to the nearest pixel.
  * Font fallback log messages now always name the correct fallback font
    family.
  * The resvg CLI no longer rounds fractional image sizes before scaling,
    and rounds the output size up instead of to the nearest integer.
  * The C API header was missing RESVG_ERROR_SVGZ_UNSUPPORTED, so all
    following error codes were off by one.
  * cargo-c now installs ResvgQt.h alongside resvg.h.

